commit 4c04e486c202c196e6c1bafb2c6da511ec5d2566

C03: a clarification asking the declared missing text is not an echo; the acknowledgement contract reads past a bare interjection (UI1647)

UI1645 measured «Type in the chat box.» answered with the right question («What text would you like me to type in the chat box?»), which UserMessagePolicy rejected as echoes_request because the short request is contained in it. When the mind declares text as the missing field and the question asks for the text, repeating the place the person named is the frame of the question, not the request handed back. In the mind, the constraint_ack contract now reads the sentence after a bare interjection («Entendido. No escribiré nada en ningún lado.»), which failed the one-sentence contract twice and turned a prohibition into a question.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


